o  could guide you and give you advice  this is different from let's say  contemporary  coaches so the subject  in the way supposes that the analyst  knows  but the analyst needs to resist uh  in that kind of confidence that he or  she  actually has knowledge about the  patient's  you know unconscious desires uh which is  why  that is a position of ignorance the  subject  you know of the analyst actually should  be  you know a little bit almost like a kind  of an idiot  someone who does not in advance  uh claim a particular kind of  knowledge and allows the subject that  analyzant  to work through his or her desires  at his of her own pace of course the  analyst will you know pose important  questions will bounce back what he or  she  hears from from the analyzant  now the other important element when we  are talking about the passion for  ignorance  is sort of the ideology it's  sort of like the kind of the social  symbolic background  in which we live the so-called big other  you know what in la canyon  psychoanalysis is called the big other  and that is institutions language  written and unwritten rules  around us and you know especially  you know in a way culture but language  as such  that uh sort of is the principle element  through the process of socialization so  here we can see that there has been you  know a kind of  a ship from you know what  uh michelle pucco was in the second half  of the 20th century  talking about when he was kind of  analyzing the relationship  between power and knowledge today  we can say that there is an important  link between  power and ignore and  you know what is happening is that on  the one hand  we have terms like knowledge based  economy which appears you know  very enlightening as if our economy  truly is based on knowledge and also  you know we might have a wrong  perception  that knowledge is sort of shared it is  easily available  to appoint it is everyone now can go  and google however behind the knowledge  that  we ge